        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm trying to identify the root behind अकुषाताम् — it's third person dual in लुङ् (aorist), and I'm considering whether it traces back to कुङ् (शब्दे), an आत्मनेपदी भ्वादि root that's अनिट्.\n\nChecking the Paninian rules on सिच् after इक्-ending roots in आत्मनेपद, I'm weighing whether सिच् would be कित् here via 1.2.11/1.2.12, or whether it stays guna-grade giving अकोष्ट. I'm also considering that कुङ् might actually belong to the कुटादि subgroup within तुदादि, which would make pratyayas ङिद्वत् per 1.2.1, affecting the final form.\n\nI recall कुङ् शब्दे sits in कुटादि (तुदादि गण), आत्मनेपदी, अनिट्, giving लुङ् forms like अकुत/अकुषाताम्/अकुषत, as opposed to भ्वादि कुङ् which would produce अकोषाताम् instead.\n\nFor लुट्, since कुटादि roots get ङिद्वत्त्व before तास् (which isn't ञित्/णित्), there's no guna, so the form becomes कुता, कुतारौ, कुतारः — confirmed by Siddhanta Kaumudi's treatment alongside नुविता and कुटिता.\n\n",
        "signature": ""
      },
